-- title:
--   Base change of a power-series quotient with nilpotent variables
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra, $\sigma$ a finite type of variables and $\iota$ an arbitrary index type, and let $\varphi : \iota \to R[\![X_\sigma]\!]$ be a family of multivariate formal power series over $R$. Write $I = (\operatorname{range}\varphi)$ for the ideal of $R[\![X_\sigma]\!]$ generated by the $\varphi_i$, and $I^S$ for the ideal of $S[\![X_\sigma]\!]$ generated by the coefficientwise images $\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ S)(\varphi_i)$. Assume there is a natural number $N$ such that $X_s^N \in I$ for every $s \in \sigma$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an isomorphism of $S$-algebras
--   $$e : S \otimes_R \bigl(R[\![X_\sigma]\!]/I\bigr) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S[\![X_\sigma]\!]/I^S$$
--   together with the compatibility that for all $s \in S$ and all $q \in R[\![X_\sigma]\!]$ one has $e(s \otimes \bar q) = s \cdot \overline{\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ S)(q)}$; that is, $e$ sends the pure tensor of $s$ with the class of $q$ to the scalar multiple by $s$ of the class of the coefficientwise image of $q$. Thus the isomorphism is pinned down on pure tensors, not merely asserted to exist.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the quotient of a formal power series ring by an ideal containing a power of each variable commutes with base change along $R \to S$; the hypothesis on the variables is what makes the quotient a finite $R$-module and is genuinely needed. It is used in the theory of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in particular for the kernel-degree calculus (composition and divisibility statements for kernels of a given degree).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_span_map_of_X_pow_mem.lean

